---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Work Authorization — JetAvenue Mobile Jet Maintenance"
  description="Submit a work authorization for mobile private jet maintenance with JetAvenue. Line MX, interior repair, avionics support. FAA-certified technicians dispatched to your aircraft."
  canonicalPath="/work-order"
>

  <section class="wo-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">GET STARTED</p>
    <h1>Work Authorization</h1>
    <p>Complete this form to authorize service. Required fields are marked with an asterisk (*).</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wo-body">
    <div class="wo-container">
      <form id="wo-form" action="https://www.recoilone.com/api/forms/work-order" method="POST" novalidate enctype="multipart/form-data">

        <!-- Routing (which brand) + hidden bot trap (renamed so autofill won't fill it) + timing + upload refs -->
        <input type="hidden" name="brand" value="jetavenue.net" />
        <input type="text" class="wo-hp" name="hp_check" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" aria-hidden="true" />
        <input type="hidden" name="fill_ms" id="wo-fillms" />
        <input type="hidden" name="uploaded_files" id="wo-uploaded" />

        <!-- ── Contact Info ── -->
        <div class="wo-row">
          <div class="wo-group">
            <label for="wo-contact">Name of Contact <span class="req">*</span></label>
            <input type="text" id="wo-contact" name="name" placeholder="Full name" required />
          </div>
          <div class="wo-group">
            <label for="wo-company">Company Name</label>
            <input type="text" id="wo-company" name="company" placeholder="Flight department or operator name" />
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="wo-group">
          <label>Billing Address <span class="req">*</span></label>
          <input type="text" name="billing_street" placeholder="Street address" required style="margin-bottom:8px" />
          <div class="wo-grid-csz">
            <input type="text" name="billing_city" placeholder="City" required />
            <input type="text" name="billing_state" placeholder="State" required />
            <input type="text" name="billing_zip" placeholder="Zip code" required />
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="wo-row">
          <div class="wo-group">
            <label for="wo-phone">Phone <span class="req">*</span></label>
            <input type="tel" id="wo-phone" name="phone" placeholder="(800) 555-0100" required />
          </div>
          <div class="wo-group">
            <label for="wo-email">Email <span class="req">*</span></label>
            <input type="email" id="wo-email" name="email" placeholder="you@example.com" required />
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="wo-row3">
          <div class="wo-group">
            <label for="wo-aircraft-type">Aircraft Type <span class="req">*</span></label>
            <input type="text" id="wo-aircraft-type" name="aircraft_type" placeholder="e.g. Gulfstream G550" required />
          </div>
          <div class="wo-group">
            <label for="wo-reg">Registration No. <span class="req">*</span></label>
            <input type="text" id="wo-reg" name="registration_number" placeholder="N12345" required />
          </div>
          <div class="wo-group">
            <label for="wo-serial">Aircraft Serial No. <span class="req">*</span></label>
            <input type="text" id="wo-serial" name="aircraft_serial" placeholder="e.g. 6050" required />
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="wo-group">
          <label>Flight Operation</label>
          <div class="wo-radios">
            <label class="radio-label"><input type="radio" name="flight_operation" value="FAR 91" /> FAR 91</label>
            <label class="radio-label"><input type="radio" name="flight_operation" value="FAR 135" /> FAR 135</label>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ── Aircraft Details (collapsible) ── -->
        <div class="wo-accordion">
          <button type="button" class="wo-accordion-btn" id="acToggle">
            <span>Aircraft Details <span class="req">*</span></span>
            <svg class="ac-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="wo-accordion-body" id="acBody">
            <div class="wo-grid-3">
              <div class="wo-group">
                <label>Engine Model No.</label>
                <input type="text" name="engine_model" placeholder="e.g. BR700" />
              </div>
              <div class="wo-group">
                <label>Aircraft Total Time <span class="req">*</span></label>
                <input type="text" name="aircraft_total_time" placeholder="Hours" required />
              </div>
              <div class="wo-group">
                <label>Aircraft Total Landings <span class="req">*</span></label>
                <input type="text" name="aircraft_total_landings" placeholder="Cycles" required />
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="wo-grid-3">
              <div class="wo-group"><label>Engine #1 S/N</label><input type="text" name="eng1_sn" /></div>
              <div class="wo-group"><label>Engine #2 S/N</label><input type="text" name="eng2_sn" /></div>
              <div class="wo-group"><label>Engine #3 S/N</label><input type="text" name="eng3_sn" /></div>
            </div>
            <div class="wo-grid-3">
              <div class="wo-group"><label>Engine #1 TT</label><input type="text" name="eng1_tt" /></div>
              <div class="wo-group"><label>Engine #2 TT</label><input type="text" name="eng2_tt" /></div>
              <div class="wo-group"><label>Engine #3 TT</label><input type="text" name="eng3_tt" /></div>
            </div>
            <div class="wo-grid-3">
              <div class="wo-group"><label>Engine #1 Cycles</label><input type="text" name="eng1_cycles" /></div>
              <div class="wo-group"><label>Engine #2 Cycles</label><input type="text" name="eng2_cycles" /></div>
              <div class="wo-group"><label>Engine #3 Cycles</label><input type="text" name="eng3_cycles" /></div>
            </div>
            <div class="wo-grid-3">
              <div class="wo-group"><label>APU Model No.</label><input type="text" name="apu_model" /></div>
              <div class="wo-group"><label>APU S/N</label><input type="text" name="apu_sn" /></div>
              <div class="wo-group"><label>APU Total Time</label><input type="text" name="apu_tt" /></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ── Service Info ── -->
        <div class="wo-row3">
          <div class="wo-group">
            <label>Is your aircraft AOG? <span class="req">*</span></label>
            <div class="wo-radios">
              <label class="radio-label"><input type="radio" name="aog" value="No" /> No</label>
              <label class="radio-label"><input type="radio" name="aog" value="Yes" /> Yes</label>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="wo-group">
            <label>Plane Locked? <span class="req">*</span></label>
            <div class="wo-radios">
              <label class="radio-label"><input type="radio" name="plane_locked" value="No" checked /> No</label>
              <label class="radio-label"><input type="radio" name="plane_locked" value="Yes" /> Yes</label>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="wo-group">
            <label>Overtime Authorized?</label>
            <div class="wo-radios">
              <label class="radio-label"><input type="radio" name="overtime" value="Yes" checked /> Yes</label>
              <label class="radio-label"><input type="radio" name="overtime" value="No" /> No</label>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="wo-group">
          <label>Location of Services (include FBO) <span class="req">*</span></label>
          <div class="wo-radios wo-radios--wrap">
            <label class="radio-label"><input type="radio" name="location" value="VNY" required /> VNY: Van Nuys</label>
            <label class="radio-label"><input type="radio" name="location" value="SDL" /> SDL: Scottsdale</label>
            <label class="radio-label"><input type="radio" name="location" value="Other" id="locOther" /> Other</label>
            <input type="text" id="locOtherText" name="location_other" placeholder="Airport / FBO…" class="loc-other-input" disabled />
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="wo-row">
          <div class="wo-group">
            <label for="wo-date">Expected Date of Departure <span class="req">*</span></label>
            <input type="date" id="wo-date" name="expected_departure" required />
          </div>
          <div class="wo-group">
            <label for="wo-po">P.O. #</label>
            <input type="text" id="wo-po" name="po_number" placeholder="#" />
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ── Document Uploads ── -->
        <div class="wo-group">
          <label>Documents</label>
          <div class="upload-zones">

            <div class="upload-zone">
              <div class="upload-zone-header">
                <span class="upload-zone-label">Work Scope <span class="req">*</span></span>
                <span class="upload-zone-note">PDF or image</span>
              </div>
              <input type="file" id="upload-sow" name="sow" accept=".pdf,image/jpeg,image/png,image/webp,image/heic,image/gif,image/tiff" multiple class="upload-input" required />
              <label for="upload-sow" class="upload-btn">Choose Files</label>
              <ul class="file-list" id="sow-list"></ul>
            </div>

            <div class="upload-zone">
              <div class="upload-zone-header">
                <span class="upload-zone-label">Photos</span>
                <span class="upload-zone-note">JPG, PNG, HEIC, WEBP, etc.</span>
              </div>
              <input type="file" id="upload-pics" name="photos" accept="image/*" multiple class="upload-input" />
              <label for="upload-pics" class="upload-btn">Choose Files</label>
              <ul class="file-list" id="pics-list"></ul>
            </div>

            <div class="upload-zone">
              <div class="upload-zone-header">
                <span class="upload-zone-label">PO</span>
                <span class="upload-zone-note">PDF or image</span>
              </div>
              <input type="file" id="upload-po" name="po" accept=".pdf,image/jpeg,image/png,image/webp,image/heic,image/gif,image/tiff" multiple class="upload-input" />
              <label for="upload-po" class="upload-btn">Choose Files</label>
              <ul class="file-list" id="po-list"></ul>
            </div>

          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="wo-group">
          <label for="wo-service">Service Required <span class="req">*</span></label>
          <textarea id="wo-service" name="service_required" rows="4" placeholder="Describe the service needed…" required></textarea>
        </div>

        <!-- ── Payment & Authorization ── -->
        <div class="wo-row-auth">
          <div class="wo-group">
            <label for="wo-payment">Method Type <span class="req">*</span></label>
            <select id="wo-payment" name="payment_method" required>
              <option value="">Please choose…</option>
              <option value="Credit Card">Credit Card</option>
              <option value="Bank/ACH">Bank / ACH Transfer</option>
              <option value="COD">COD</option>
            </select>
          </div>
          <div class="wo-group">
            <label for="wo-authorized-by">Service Authorized By <span class="req">*</span></label>
            <input type="text" id="wo-authorized-by" name="authorized_by" placeholder="Full name of authorizing party" required />
          </div>
          <div class="wo-group">
            <label for="wo-auth-date">Date <span class="req">*</span></label>
            <input type="date" id="wo-auth-date" name="authorization_date" required />
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ── Credit Card details (shown only when Method Type = Credit Card) ── -->
        <div class="wo-cc" id="cc-fields" hidden>
          <p class="cc-note">Provide the cardholder details below. For your security we never collect the card number, expiration, or CVV. Those are arranged with Jet Avenue directly.</p>
          <p class="cc-error" id="cc-error" hidden></p>
          <div class="wo-group">
            <label>Card Type <span class="req">*</span></label>
            <div class="wo-radios">
              <label class="radio-label"><input type="radio" name="cc_type" value="Visa" /> Visa</label>
              <label class="radio-label"><input type="radio" name="cc_type" value="Mastercard" /> Mastercard</label>
              <label class="radio-label"><input type="radio" name="cc_type" value="Amex" /> Amex</label>
              <label class="radio-label"><input type="radio" name="cc_type" value="Discover" /> Discover</label>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="wo-row">
            <div class="wo-group">
              <label for="cc-name">Name on Card <span class="req">*</span></label>
              <input type="text" id="cc-name" name="cc_name" placeholder="Cardholder name" />
            </div>
            <div class="wo-group">
              <label for="cc-phone">Cardholder Phone <span class="req">*</span></label>
              <input type="tel" id="cc-phone" name="cc_phone" placeholder="(800) 555-0100" />
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="wo-group">
            <label>Cardholder Billing Address <span class="req">*</span></label>
            <input type="text" name="cc_billing_street" placeholder="Street address" style="margin-bottom:8px" />
            <div class="wo-grid-csz">
              <input type="text" name="cc_billing_city" placeholder="City" />
              <input type="text" name="cc_billing_state" placeholder="State" />
              <input type="text" name="cc_billing_zip" placeholder="Zip code" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ── Terms & Conditions (full text opens in the modal; agreement recorded on submit) ── -->
        <div class="wo-tc-row" id="termsgroup">
          <span class="wo-tc-title">Jet Avenue Inc. Terms &amp; Conditions <span class="req">*</span></span>
          <button type="button" class="wo-review-btn" id="reviewTerms">Review Terms &amp; Conditions</button>
          <span class="wo-tc-agreed" id="termsAgreedBadge">&#10003; Terms accepted</span>
          <input type="hidden" name="terms_agreed" id="wo-terms" value="" />
        </div>

        <div class="wo-overlay" id="termsOverlay" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="wo-modal" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="termsTitle">
            <div class="wo-modal-head">
              <h2 id="termsTitle">Terms &amp; Conditions</h2>
              <button type="button" class="wo-modal-x" id="termsClose" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
            </div>
            <div class="wo-modal-body" id="termsBody">

            <p class="tc-section">WORK AUTHORIZATION AGREEMENT TERMS AND CONDITIONS</p>

            <p class="tc-section">SECTION 1 — DEFINITIONS AND BINDING EFFECT</p>

            <p>These Standard Terms and Conditions of Engagement (the "Terms"), together with any executed Work Order, Service Authorization, or appended schedule, form the complete and exclusive agreement (the "Engagement Agreement") between JET AVENUE INC ("JET AVENUE INC") and the aircraft owner, operator, or authorized representative identified in the applicable Work Order ("Client"). All labor, parts, consumables, and technical services furnished hereunder are collectively referred to as "Maintenance Services." The aircraft identified in the applicable Work Order is referred to as the "Subject Aircraft." "JET AVENUE INC Parties" means JET AVENUE INC and each of its principals, employees, independent contractors, agents, and designees performing any portion of the Maintenance Services. All Maintenance Services are performed on a mobile basis at a mutually agreed-upon location designated in the Work Order (the "Service Location"); JET AVENUE INC does not operate a fixed repair facility, and no provision of these Terms shall be construed to imply otherwise. JET AVENUE INC's access to, movement of, or temporary control over the Subject Aircraft for the limited purpose of performing, facilitating, inspecting, documenting, or completing Maintenance Services shall not be construed as general storage, long-term custody, or acceptance of responsibility for the Subject Aircraft except to the extent expressly stated in this Agreement or required by applicable law. This Engagement Agreement is the parties' entire understanding and displaces all prior oral or written representations, negotiations, or commitments. Amendments are effective only if in writing, signed by authorized representatives of both parties, and expressly identified as modifications to this Engagement Agreement, except for scope and overtime adjustments as provided herein.</p>

            <p class="tc-section">SECTION 2 — AUTHORIZATION OF SERVICES AND SCOPE CHANGES</p>

            <p>By executing a Work Order or otherwise requesting Maintenance Services, Client irrevocably authorizes JET AVENUE INC to furnish all labor and materials reasonably necessary to accomplish the agreed scope of work. Scope expansions, change orders, and overtime requests may be authorized verbally by Client or Client's designated representative and shall be binding upon such authorization; no written confirmation is required. Client's tender of payment — in whole or in part — for any service line item shall constitute Client's conclusive, non-retractable acknowledgment that such item was duly authorized and performed. JET AVENUE INC shall have no obligation to seek further confirmation before proceeding with work that, in JET AVENUE INC's reasonable professional judgment, is necessary for airworthiness or safety, and Client shall be responsible for all associated charges.</p>

            <p class="tc-section">SECTION 3 — BILLING BASIS, ESTIMATES, AND RATE SCHEDULE</p>

            <p>All Maintenance Services shall be invoiced on a time-and-materials basis ("T&amp;M") unless a separate fixed-price authorization has been fully executed in writing by both parties and expressly incorporates these Terms. Any labor-hour projections, cost estimates, parts forecasts, or completion timelines communicated by JET AVENUE INC — whether in writing or verbally — are provided solely as non-binding planning references. They do not constitute price guarantees, cost caps, or representations of final cost, and Client shall not rely on them as such. Labor shall be billed at the rates set forth in JET AVENUE INC's then-current Labor Rate Schedule / Aviation Maintenance Services Rate Card in effect on the date the work is performed. Client acknowledges that the applicable rate schedule may include scheduled, unscheduled, priority/AOG, after-hours, holiday, travel time, standby time, minimum call-out, consumables, shop supply, parts, materials, freight, and other charges. Component exchange charges, core fees, and shop supply charges may be invoiced separately. JET AVENUE INC reserves the right to adjust rates upon reasonable notice.</p>

            <p class="tc-section">SECTION 4 — PAYMENT TERMS, DEPOSITS, AND AIRCRAFT LIEN</p>

            <p>Invoices are due net thirty (30) days from the date of issuance for Clients holding approved credit accounts, unless a shorter payment period is stated in the applicable Work Order, proposal, invoice, or written authorization. Clients without established credit shall pay all amounts in advance, by deposit, upon demand, or before release of the Subject Aircraft, as determined by JET AVENUE INC.</p>

            <p>For engagements estimated to exceed Ten Thousand Dollars ($10,000.00) but not exceeding Thirty Thousand Dollars ($30,000.00), Client shall remit an initial mobilization deposit of fifty percent (50%) of the estimated value before commencement. For engagements estimated to exceed Thirty Thousand Dollars ($30,000.00), JET AVENUE INC may require an initial deposit, progress payments, parts deposits, milestone payments, or other payment arrangements stated in the applicable Work Order, proposal, invoice, or written authorization. Deposits are earned upon receipt to compensate JET AVENUE INC for mobilization, scheduling, administrative preparation, travel readiness, procurement efforts, reserved labor capacity, and related costs, and may be applied against amounts ultimately invoiced.</p>

            <p>Deposits for special-order, long-lead, non-returnable, exchange, custom, or Client-specific parts, materials, components, vendor services, or subcontractor services are non-refundable except to the extent JET AVENUE INC actually receives a refund or credit from the applicable vendor or subcontractor. Client remains responsible for cancellation charges, restocking fees, freight, shipping, handling, core charges, vendor charges, subcontractor charges, and other costs incurred or committed in reliance on Client's authorization.</p>

            <p>JET AVENUE INC may issue interim invoices and may demand additional deposits or progress payments upon material scope growth, unanticipated cost escalation, parts procurement, extended troubleshooting, AOG requirements, subcontractor involvement, or other circumstances increasing the cost or risk of the engagement. Maintenance Services may be suspended without liability to JET AVENUE INC until required payments are received.</p>

            <p>Client shall pay all undisputed amounts when due regardless of any pending dispute over other line items. Any objection to an invoice, charge, labor entry, part, material, travel charge, subcontractor charge, or other billed item must be made in writing within fifteen (15) days after the invoice date and must describe the basis of the dispute in reasonable detail. Any item not disputed within such period shall be deemed accepted and approved for payment. Acceptance of partial payment, delayed payment, or payment under protest shall not constitute a waiver of any amount due, late charge, interest, lien right, collection right, or other remedy available to JET AVENUE INC. Client shall remain obligated to timely pay all undisputed amounts. JET AVENUE INC shall not be obligated to release the Subject Aircraft, installed components, removed components, logbook entries, maintenance releases, parts, materials, or records generated by JET AVENUE INC until all amounts then due to JET AVENUE INC have been paid in full, except to the extent prohibited by applicable law.</p>

            <p>To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, JET AVENUE INC reserves and asserts all lien, possessory, repairman, mechanic, artisan, storage, materialman, and collection rights available with respect to the Subject Aircraft, installed components, removed components, parts, materials, accessories, records, and related property for all unpaid charges. Client consents to JET AVENUE INC's exercise, perfection, recording, enforcement, and foreclosure of such rights as permitted by applicable law.</p>

            <p>Past-due balances shall accrue interest at one and one-half percent (5 %) per month, or the maximum rate permitted by law, whichever is less, together with all attorneys' fees, collection costs, lien recording costs, enforcement costs, court costs, arbitration costs, and other expenses incurred in recovery.</p>

            <p class="tc-section">SECTION 5 — TAX OBLIGATIONS</p>

            <p>Client is solely responsible for all federal, state, local, and international taxes, duties, tariffs, levies, and surcharges ("Tax Obligations") applicable to the Maintenance Services, labor, materials, parts, consumables, transportation, freight, shipping, travel, subcontractor services, vendor services, or any other amounts billed under this Engagement Agreement, excluding only JET AVENUE INC's own net income taxes. Client shall indemnify and hold JET AVENUE INC Parties harmless for any Tax Obligations that become due and are attributable to Client's engagement. All contract amounts are exclusive of Tax Obligations. If applicable law requires Client to withhold tax from any payment, Client shall gross up the payment so that JET AVENUE INC receives the full amount as if no withholding applied.</p>

            <p class="tc-section">SECTION 6 — LIMITED WARRANTY; EXCLUSIVE REMEDIES</p>

            <p><strong>6.1 Scope of Warranty</strong></p>

            <p>JET AVENUE INC warrants that Maintenance Services will be performed in material conformity with applicable manufacturer maintenance manuals, service instructions, and airworthiness directives in effect on the date of performance. With respect to parts and materials supplied by JET AVENUE INC, JET AVENUE INC does not provide any independent manufacturer, design, merchantability, fitness, or airworthiness warranty, but will pass through to Client any assignable manufacturer, vendor, or supplier warranty actually available to JET AVENUE INC. This warranty is personal to the client and is non-transferable. It expires upon the earlier of: (a) one (1) month from the date of completion of the applicable Work Order; or (b) one hundred (100) flight hours following such completion date. Any warranty period applicable to parts, components, or materials supplied by a manufacturer, vendor, subcontractor, or third-party supplier shall be governed solely by that manufacturer's, vendor's, subcontractor's, or supplier's warranty terms, if any. The warranty does not extend to pre-existing conditions, pre-existing wear or corrosion, hidden defects not discoverable through standard inspection practices, or any condition caused or contributed to by Client or a third party after delivery. No warranty is provided with respect to any Client-supplied, owner-supplied, operator-supplied, used, overhauled, repaired, exchanged, or third-party-supplied part, component, material, accessory, or equipment. Client is solely responsible for all warranty claims, compatibility issues, documentation issues, removal, replacement, reinstallation, freight, downtime, and labor costs associated with any such item, except to the extent caused by JET AVENUE INC's proven defective installation.</p>

            <p><strong>6.2 Sole and Exclusive Remedies</strong></p>

            <p>Upon a timely, valid warranty claim, JET AVENUE INC's entire obligation — and Client's sole and exclusive remedy — shall be, at JET AVENUE INC's sole election: (i) re-performance of the nonconforming work at a mutually agreed-upon location; (ii) replacement of defective JET AVENUE INC-supplied parts, provided that JET AVENUE INC shall have no obligation to provide warranty remedies for defects attributable to manufacturers, vendors, subcontractors, owner-supplied parts, customer-supplied parts, or third-party components beyond any warranty rights actually assignable to Client; or (iii) issuance of a credit toward future Maintenance Services in the amount of the labor charged for the nonconforming work. JET AVENUE INC shall bear reasonable labor costs directly associated with remedial work, provided Client returns the Subject Aircraft to a mutually agreed-upon Service Location at Client's sole expense. JET AVENUE INC shall have no obligation to provide warranty remedies at any other location and shall not be responsible for any ferry flight costs, repositioning expenses, third-party labor, or consequential costs. For warranty claims arising from inspection Services, Client's sole remedy is a refund of the direct labor charge for that specific inspection task. Under no circumstances shall JET AVENUE INC's aggregate warranty liability exceed the total labor fees actually paid by Client to JET AVENUE INC under the applicable Work Order giving rise to the warranty claim.</p>

            <p><strong>6.3 Aircraft Damage — Limitation of Remedy</strong></p>

            <p>6.3.1 In the limited circumstance where JET AVENUE INC's direct, proven negligence — not mere error of judgment or inspection oversight — is the proximate and predominant cause of physical damage to the Subject Aircraft during active performance of Maintenance Services, and Client provides written notice within thirty (30) days of discovery, JET AVENUE INC's maximum obligation shall be to repair the documented damage at a mutually agreed-upon Service Location using methods selected by JET AVENUE INC in its sole discretion. If JET AVENUE INC determines, in its reasonable judgment, that the damage renders the aircraft beyond economical repair, JET AVENUE INC's entire liability shall be capped at the lesser of: (a) the pre-damage fair market value of the Subject Aircraft as established by an independent USPAP-certified appraiser selected by JET AVENUE INC; or (b) the total fees paid by Client on all Work Orders with JET AVENUE INC in the preceding twelve (12) months. Receipt of any payment under this clause requires Client to transfer clear, unencumbered title to the Subject Aircraft to JET AVENUE INC.</p>

            <p>6.3.2 The remedy in Section 6.3.1 is wholly inapplicable to: (a) any damage not reported in writing within thirty (30) days of discovery; (b) damage that manifests or is discovered after Client has accepted the Aircraft and departed the Service Location; (c) damage caused in whole or in part by pre-existing conditions, third-party acts, Client's own personnel, or FBO ground handling; (d) any Ground Handling Event, defined as any occurrence during aircraft movement, towing, taxiing, ramp operations, or any ground contact event involving the Aircraft; or (e) damage to avionics, interior, or paint attributable to normal maintenance access. JET AVENUE INC's liability for any single incident is capped at Five Million Dollars ($5,000,000.00) in the aggregate, regardless of the number of claims arising from that incident.</p>

            <p><strong>6.4 Warranty Voidance</strong></p>

            <p>Warranty rights under this Section 6 shall be void with respect to the affected work, part, component, system, or condition if: (i) the Subject Aircraft or affected component has been operated, maintained, stored, or modified in any manner inconsistent with manufacturer specifications after delivery; (ii) any third party has performed work on, modified, inspected, adjusted, removed, reinstalled, or disturbed the affected work, part, component, system, or condition after delivery; (iii) Client fails to comply strictly with the notice and return requirements of Section 6.5; or (iv) Client has any outstanding unpaid balance with JET AVENUE INC at the time the claim is submitted unless the unpaid balance is disputed in good faith and the warranty claim is unrelated to the disputed charge.</p>

            <p><strong>6.5 Warranty Claim Procedure — Strict Compliance Required</strong></p>

            <p>Warranty rights are conditioned upon Client's strict compliance with all of the following, each of which is a condition precedent to any warranty obligation of JET AVENUE INC: (i) written notice of the alleged defect delivered to JET AVENUE INC within thirty (30) days of discovery; (ii) Client's return or disposition of the affected component as directed by JET AVENUE INC within twenty-one (21) days of JET AVENUE INC's instructions; (iii) Client's production of all flight logs, maintenance records, CVR/FDR data, and operational data, to the extent available and reasonably related to the alleged defect, reasonably requested by JET AVENUE INC; and (iv) Client's account with JET AVENUE INC must be current with no past-due balance. Failure to satisfy any single condition precedent operates as a complete waiver of the applicable warranty claim.</p>

            <p class="tc-section">SECTION 7 — COMPLETE DISCLAIMER OF ALL OTHER WARRANTIES</p>

            <p>THE LIMITED WARRANTY IN SECTION 6 IS THE ONLY WARRANTY JET AVENUE INC PROVIDES. EXCEPT AS EXPRESSLY STATED IN SECTION 6, ALL OTHER WARRANTIES — EXPRESS, IMPLIED, STATUTORY, OR ARISING BY COURSE OF DEALING, COURSE OF PERFORMANCE, OR USAGE OF TRADE — ARE HEREBY DISCLAIMED IN THEIR ENTIRETY, INCLUDING WITHOUT LIMITATION: ANY IMPLIED WARRANTY OF MERCHANTABILITY; ANY IMPLIED WARRANTY OF FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE; ANY IMPLIED WARRANTY OF AIRWORTHINESS OR FLIGHT SAFETY; ANY WARRANTY ARISING UNDER ANY FEDERAL AVIATION REGULATION; AND ANY WARRANTY OF WORKMANLIKE PERFORMANCE BEYOND THAT EXPRESSLY STATED IN SECTION 6.1. CLIENT ACKNOWLEDGES THAT IT IS A SOPHISTICATED COMMERCIAL PARTY, THAT IT HAS HAD THE OPPORTUNITY TO NEGOTIATE THESE TERMS, AND THAT THE DISCLAIMER OF IMPLIED WARRANTIES IS A MATERIAL PART OF THE BARGAINED-FOR EXCHANGE. CLIENT, ON BEHALF OF ITSELF, ITS INSURER, AND ALL PARTIES CLAIMING THROUGH CLIENT, WAIVES ALL CLAIMS BASED ON DISCLAIMED WARRANTIES, STRICT PRODUCTS LIABILITY, OR ANY WARRANTY THEORY OTHER THAN THE LIMITED EXPRESS WARRANTY SET FORTH IN SECTION 6. THIS DISCLAIMER IS ENFORCEABLE TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY CALIFORNIA LAW.</p>

            <p class="tc-section">SECTION 8 — AGGREGATE LIABILITY CAP AND CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES WAIVER</p>

            <p>8.1 AGGREGATE CAP. JET AVENUE INC'S TOTAL CUMULATIVE LIABILITY TO CLIENT UNDER OR RELATED TO THIS ENGAGEMENT AGREEMENT, FROM ALL CAUSES OF ACTION COMBINED AND UNDER ANY LEGAL THEORY, SHALL NOT EXCEED THE TOTAL LABOR FEES ACTUALLY PAID BY CLIENT TO JET AVENUE INC UNDER THE SPECIFIC WORK ORDER GIVING RISE TO THE CLAIM. THIS CAP APPLIES REGARDLESS OF THE NUMBER OF CLAIMS, INCIDENTS, OR THEORIES OF RECOVERY.</p>

            <p>8.2 CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES WAIVER. UNDER NO CIRCUMSTANCES SHALL JET AVENUE INC PARTIES BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, PUNITIVE, EXEMPLARY, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES OF ANY NATURE WHATSOEVER, WHETHER ARISING IN CONTRACT, WARRANTY, TORT, NEGLIGENCE, STRICT LIABILITY, STATUTE, REGULATION, INDEMNITY, OR OTHERWISE, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO: LOSS OF USE OF THE SUBJECT AIRCRAFT; LOST CHARTER OR RENTAL REVENUE; TRIP CANCELLATION COSTS; PASSENGER INCONVENIENCE; INCREASED OPERATING OR REPOSITIONING EXPENSES; LOSS OF PROFITS OR BUSINESS OPPORTUNITIES; DIMINUTION IN AIRCRAFT VALUE; REPUTATIONAL HARM; OR ANY SIMILAR ECONOMIC LOSS. THIS WAIVER APPLIES REGARDLESS OF WHETHER JET AVENUE INC WAS ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES AND REGARDLESS OF THE LEGAL THEORY ASSERTED.</p>

            <p>8.3 SURVIVAL AND INDEPENDENCE. THE LIABILITY CAP IN SECTION 8.1 AND THE CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES WAIVER IN SECTION 8.2 ARE INDEPENDENT OF ALL WARRANTY PROVISIONS, SURVIVE THE EXPIRATION OR TERMINATION OF THIS ENGAGEMENT AGREEMENT, AND SHALL REMAIN ENFORCEABLE EVEN IF ANY LIMITED REMEDY IS FOUND TO HAVE FAILED OF ITS ESSENTIAL PURPOSE.</p>

            <p class="tc-section">SECTION 9 — INSURANCE; SUBROGATION WAIVER</p>

            <p>Client shall, at its own expense, maintain in force throughout the engagement and for a period of no less than two (2) years thereafter: (a) aircraft hull and liability insurance covering the Subject Aircraft for not less than its full agreed value, with a minimum of Five Million Dollars ($5,000,000.00) in liability coverage per occurrence; and (b) any other insurance required by applicable law. Such insurance shall be primary and non-contributory with respect to any insurance maintained by JET AVENUE INC Parties, and shall respond before any insurance available to JET AVENUE INC Parties. Client shall cause its insurer to include JET AVENUE INC as an additional insured on all such policies and to provide a waiver of subrogation in favor of JET AVENUE INC Parties on all coverages. Client shall furnish certificates of insurance and, upon request, applicable endorsements evidencing such coverage, additional insured status, waiver of subrogation, and primary and non-contributory coverage before commencement of Maintenance Services and at any time upon request. If Client fails to maintain required insurance, JET AVENUE INC may, but shall not be obligated to, suspend Maintenance Services without liability. Client's insurer shall have no right of subrogation against JET AVENUE INC Parties for any claim paid under Client's policies, and Client shall include a contractual subrogation waiver in all applicable insurance policies. To the extent Client's insurer pays any claim and asserts subrogation rights contrary to this Section, Client shall indemnify JET AVENUE INC Parties against such subrogated claim.</p>

            <p class="tc-section">SECTION 10 — MUTUAL RELEASE UPON AIRCRAFT ACCEPTANCE</p>

            <p>Client's execution of any Work Order completion acknowledgment, departure from the Service Location following completion of Maintenance Services, or commencement of flight operations following the applicable Work Order shall constitute Client's irrevocable acceptance of all Maintenance Services performed under that Work Order and a full release of JET AVENUE INC Parties from all claims, known and unknown, arising from or related to that Work Order, except only for warranty claims submitted in strict compliance with Section 6.5. Client waives any right to assert claims discovered after acceptance that could have been discovered through reasonable diligence at the time of acceptance. This release is a material inducement to JET AVENUE INC's provision of services at the agreed rates. JET AVENUE INC's commencement or continuation of Maintenance Services without receipt of certificates, endorsements, or other proof of insurance shall not waive Client's insurance obligations or limit Client's indemnity obligations under this Engagement Agreement.</p>

            <p class="tc-section">SECTION 11 — CLIENT INDEMNIFICATION AND HOLD HARMLESS</p>

            <p>Client shall indemnify, defend with counsel acceptable to JET AVENUE INC, and hold harmless JET AVENUE INC Parties from and against any and all third-party claims, suits, demands, losses, damages, fines, penalties, and expenses (including reasonable attorneys' fees and costs through all appeals) arising out of or related to: (a) Client's ownership, operation, use, maintenance history, condition, airworthiness status, storage, transportation, movement, or presence of the Subject Aircraft at or near the Service Location; (b) the acts or omissions of Client's employees, agents, passengers, or subcontractors at or near the Service Location; (c) Client's breach of any obligation under this Engagement Agreement; (d) any claim by Client's insurer or any subrogating party against JET AVENUE INC in violation of Section 9; (e) any violation of export control, customs, or import regulations by Client; (f) any third-party claim alleging that the Subject Aircraft was not airworthy, unless a final, non-appealable judgment establishes that JET AVENUE INC's gross negligence was the sole proximate cause; (g) any claim, damage, delay, loss, injury, airworthiness issue, regulatory issue, or economic loss arising from Client-supplied, owner-supplied, operator-supplied, vendor-supplied, exchanged, overhauled, repaired, or third-party-supplied parts, components, materials, equipment, records, or documentation; (h) any claim arising from a pre-purchase inspection, maintenance evaluation, records review, discrepancy list, maintenance recommendation, or inspection report prepared by JET AVENUE INC, except to the extent a final, non-appealable judgment establishes that such claim resulted solely from the gross negligence or willful misconduct of JET AVENUE INC. This indemnification obligation survives completion of the Maintenance Services and the termination or expiration of this Engagement Agreement.</p>

            <p class="tc-section">SECTION 12 — PERSONAL PROPERTY; NO BAILMENT</p>

            <p>JET AVENUE INC assumes no responsibility, custody, or care for any personal property, crew effects, cabin equipment, catering, removable property, loose equipment, baggage, documents, valuables, electronic devices, or non-certificated items brought to the Service Location by Client or Client's representatives, unless JET AVENUE INC expressly agrees in writing to accept responsibility for such item. No bailment relationship is created with respect to any such personal property or non-aircraft items by this Engagement Agreement, JET AVENUE INC's performance of Maintenance Services, or JET AVENUE INC's proximity to such items. JET AVENUE INC may direct the Client to remove any items it deems hazardous or inappropriate. Client shall indemnify JET AVENUE INC Parties against all claims arising from such personal property or non-aircraft items.</p>

            <p class="tc-section">SECTION 13 — NO DELAY LIABILITY; FORCE MAJEURE</p>

            <p>JET AVENUE INC shall use commercially reasonable efforts to complete Maintenance Services within communicated timeframes. Overtime is excluded from commercially reasonable efforts unless Client has separately agreed in writing to bear premium labor charges. JET AVENUE INC shall not be liable for delay damages, penalties, ferry costs, loss of use, or consequential losses attributable to schedule changes under any circumstances, including delays arising from parts availability, additional discrepancies, regulatory requirements, customer approvals, subcontractor availability, weather, airport operations, or other causes not solely within JET AVENUE INC's direct control.</p>

            <p>JET AVENUE INC shall not be in default and shall have no liability for delays or non-performance caused by events beyond its reasonable control, including but not limited to: parts or materials unavailability or supply chain disruption; manufacturer or vendor delays; Client delay, Client's failure to provide records, approvals, access, parts, information, authorizations, payment, or insurance documentation; FBO delay; airport authority delay; third-party contractor delay; inclement weather or acts of God; labor disputes; FAA or regulatory actions; inspection findings, newly discovered discrepancies, airworthiness concerns, required corrective actions, required testing, required documentation, return-to-service issues; travel restrictions; equipment failure; or any other circumstance outside JET AVENUE INC's direct operational control ("Force Majeure Event"). JET AVENUE INC shall notify Client of a Force Majeure Event within a reasonable time and shall resume performance as soon as practicable.</p>

            <p class="tc-section">SECTION 14 — DELIVERY, ACCEPTANCE, AND AIRCRAFT RELEASE</p>

            <p>Upon JET AVENUE INC's notification of completion, Client shall promptly arrange collection of the Subject Aircraft from the Service Location. Client shall have the opportunity to conduct an acceptance inspection prior to departure of the Subject Aircraft. Departure of the Subject Aircraft from the Service Location, commencement of engine start, or any post-completion flight operation shall constitute irrevocable acceptance of all Maintenance Services under the applicable Work Order, except for warranty claims properly asserted pursuant to Section 6. JET AVENUE INC shall not be obligated to release the Subject Aircraft until full payment of all outstanding amounts has been received. Title to all JET AVENUE INC-supplied parts and materials installed in the Subject Aircraft vests in Client only upon receipt of payment in full. JET AVENUE INC reserves a purchase-money security interest and all other rights available under applicable law with respect to any unpaid parts, materials, components, accessories, and equipment supplied by JET AVENUE INC.</p>

            <p class="tc-section">SECTION 15 — AIRCRAFT ON PREMISES; STORAGE</p>

            <p>If the Subject Aircraft remains at the Service Location beyond five (5) calendar days following JET AVENUE INC's notification of completion — for any reason, including non-payment, Client delay, lack of required approvals, lack of flight crew, weather, airport restrictions, or Client's failure to arrange removal — Client shall be assessed a daily delay, ramp, storage, or administrative fee of not less than Three Hundred Dollars ($300.00) per day, or the prevailing market rate for comparable aircraft storage, ramp occupancy, or administrative delay at that location, whichever is greater. Storage fees begin accruing on the sixth (6th) day without further notice. Any deterioration, damage, loss, airport charge, FBO charge, ramp fee, storage fee, regulatory consequence, inspection requirement, calendar-time item, maintenance requirement, or operational consequence arising during such period shall be Client's sole responsibility.</p>

            <p class="tc-section">SECTION 16 — INSPECTION DISCLAIMER</p>

            <p>Client acknowledges and agrees that: (a) inspection Services are designed to identify conditions visible or detectable through standard, non-destructive inspection methods in use at the time and within the scope specifically authorized by Client; (b) JET AVENUE INC does not warrant that any inspection will detect all existing defects, latent conditions, or hidden damage; (c) a satisfactory inspection result does not constitute a warranty of airworthiness or fitness for flight, value, marketability, title, damage history, logbook completeness, regulatory compliance, or future condition; and (d) the discovery of additional defects or discrepancies during or after an inspection, whether or not detected by JET AVENUE INC, shall not give rise to any claim against JET AVENUE INC unless JET AVENUE INC's gross negligence is established by clear and convincing evidence. Pre-purchase inspections, records reviews, discrepancy lists, maintenance evaluations, and similar services are limited-scope advisory services only and are not guarantees of the Subject Aircraft's airworthiness, value, condition, conformity, marketability, title status, damage history, maintenance history, regulatory compliance, or suitability for Client's intended use. Client releases JET AVENUE INC Parties from all claims arising from undetected conditions in aircraft inspected under any Work Order.</p>

            <p class="tc-section">SECTION 17 — SAFETY, FACILITY COMPLIANCE, AND CLIENT CONDUCT</p>

            <p>Client and all Client-affiliated personnel present at the Service Location shall comply with all applicable safety protocols, FBO regulations, airport authority rules, TSA/security requirements, ramp access requirements, fuel farm restrictions, customs requirements, hangar rules, insurance requirements, and any reasonable directions issued by JET AVENUE INC. JET AVENUE INC may suspend Maintenance Services, remove personnel, decline access, or require Client-affiliated personnel to leave the Service Location if JET AVENUE INC reasonably determines that any unsafe, disruptive, noncompliant, or unauthorized condition exists. Client assumes all risk of injury or loss arising from its presence at the Service Location and agrees to indemnify JET AVENUE INC Parties against all claims arising from Client personnel's actions, omissions, presence, directions, interference, unauthorized access, or failure to comply with applicable rules or JET AVENUE INC's reasonable directions at or near the Service Location, except where caused solely by JET AVENUE INC's gross negligence.</p>

            <p class="tc-section">SECTION 18 — DISPUTE RESOLUTION; GOVERNING LAW; CLASS ACTION WAIVER</p>

            <p>All disputes arising under or related to this Engagement Agreement shall be resolved exclusively by binding arbitration administered by the American Arbitration Association ("AAA") under its Commercial Arbitration Rules, as modified herein. Arbitration shall be conducted in Los Angeles County, California, before a single arbitrator unless the amount in controversy exceeds Two Million Dollars ($2,000,000.00), in which case a panel of three (3) arbitrators shall be appointed in accordance with the AAA Commercial Arbitration Rules. Notwithstanding the foregoing, JET AVENUE INC may pursue any action or proceeding in a court of competent jurisdiction for temporary, preliminary, or permanent injunctive relief, lien enforcement, repossession, replevin, collection of undisputed amounts, protection of confidential information, or enforcement of any arbitration award. For any court proceeding permitted under this Section, Client irrevocably consents to the exclusive jurisdiction and venue of the state and federal courts located in Broward County, CALIFORNIA.</p>

            <p>EACH PARTY IRREVOCABLY WAIVES ANY RIGHT TO PARTICIPATE IN ANY CLASS, COLLECTIVE, OR REPRESENTATIVE ARBITRATION OR LITIGATION PROCEEDING. ALL CLAIMS MUST BE BROUGHT IN THE PARTY'S INDIVIDUAL CAPACITY.</p>

            <p>Discovery in arbitration shall be limited to ten (10) document requests and two (2) depositions per side absent agreement or arbitrator order. The arbitrator shall have no authority to award punitive or exemplary damages. The arbitrator's award shall be final and binding, and judgment may be entered in any court of competent jurisdiction. This Engagement Agreement is governed by the laws of the State of CALIFORNIA, without application of conflict-of-law rules. The U.N. Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of Goods is excluded. The prevailing party in any arbitration or court proceeding permitted under this Section shall be entitled to recover its reasonable attorneys' fees, expert fees, arbitration fees, court costs, and enforcement costs.</p>

            <p class="tc-section">SECTION 19 — GENERAL PROVISIONS</p>

            <p>If any provision hereof is found unenforceable, it shall be modified to the minimum extent necessary to make it enforceable, and all other provisions remain in full force. These Terms govern over any conflicting provision in any incorporated document unless such document expressly overrides a specific numbered section. "Include" and "including" are non-limiting. Client shall comply, and shall cause its owners, operators, representatives, agents, crews, vendors, and subcontractors to comply, with all applicable U.S. export control, sanctions, customs, import, re-export, anti-bribery, anti-corruption, and ITAR regulations. No waiver of any right shall be implied from a party's failure to exercise such right. JET AVENUE INC may assign this Engagement Agreement or any Work Order without Client's consent. Client may not assign without JET AVENUE INC's prior written approval. Notices to Client may also be delivered to any email address, mailing address, billing contact, operational contact, or representative provided by Client or used by Client in connection with the applicable Work Order. Electronic signatures, scanned signatures, PDF signatures, click-through approvals, email approvals, text-message approvals, and other electronically verifiable approvals shall be deemed originals and shall be binding for all purposes. This Engagement Agreement, including these Terms, the applicable Work Order, any executed Service Authorization, and any incorporated rate schedule or schedule of services, constitutes the entire agreement between the parties with respect to the subject matter hereof and supersedes all prior or contemporaneous oral or written proposals, estimates, negotiations, representations, understandings, and agreements. No prior or contemporaneous statement, representation, estimate, course of dealing, or trade practice shall modify, supplement, or vary the express terms of this Engagement Agreement. This Engagement Agreement and any dispute, claim, or controversy arising out of or relating to this Engagement Agreement, the Maintenance Services, the Subject Aircraft, or the parties' relationship shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of CALIFORNIA, without regard to conflict-of-law principles.</p>

            <p class="tc-section">SECTION 20 — AUTHORITY; JOINT AND SEVERAL LIABILITY</p>

            <p>The individual executing this Engagement Agreement or any Work Order on behalf of Client represents and warrants that such individual is fully authorized to bind Client and, where applicable, all registered owners, lessors, and lessees of the Subject Aircraft to all obligations hereunder. Such individual and Client shall be jointly and severally liable for all payment and indemnification obligations under this Engagement Agreement. Client warrants that it holds all necessary authorizations to present the Subject Aircraft for maintenance and that no third-party consent is required that has not already been obtained.</p>

            <p class="tc-section">PROPOSAL ACCEPTANCE</p>

            <p>This Proposal is expressly conditioned upon and incorporates JET AVENUE INC's Standard Terms and Conditions of Engagement set forth above, which Client acknowledges having read and understood.</p>

            <p>Upon Client's written acceptance, JET AVENUE INC will issue a formal Work Order enumerating all approved tasks. The executed Work Order, together with these Terms, shall constitute the definitive binding agreement and shall supersede this Proposal and all prior communications. In the event of any conflict, these Terms shall control unless the applicable Work Order expressly identifies the specific section of these Terms being modified and states that such modification is intended to control.</p>

            <p class="tc-section">QUOTE VALIDITY AND AUTHORIZATION REQUIREMENTS</p>

            <p>Pricing in this Proposal is valid for thirty (30) days from the date of issuance and is subject to revision upon parts pricing changes or material scope modifications.</p>

            <p>Maintenance Services shall not commence until all of the following have been received by JET AVENUE INC:</p>

            <p>• Fully executed Proposal or other written authorization returned by Client and accepted by JET AVENUE INC<br />
            • Executed Work Order and material call-out authorization<br />
            • Required deposit or initial progress payment per Section 4<br />
            • Certificates of insurance and endorsements required under Section 9</p>

            <p class="tc-section">CONFIDENTIALITY</p>

            <p>All pricing, labor estimates, methodologies, technical data, and supporting materials in this Proposal are proprietary to JET AVENUE INC. This Proposal is furnished solely to enable Client's evaluation of proposed Maintenance Services. Client shall not disclose, copy, or distribute any portion of this Proposal to any third party without prior written consent from JET AVENUE INC, except as required for Client's internal review, legal counsel review, or regulatory compliance. Clients shall be responsible for any disclosure by its owners, operators, employees, agents, representatives, advisors, lenders, insurers, brokers, or consultants. Any breach of this confidentiality obligation shall entitle JET AVENUE INC to seek injunctive relief without bond in addition to all other available remedies.</p>

            <p class="tc-section">NOTICE</p>

            <p>TERMS ARE DUE UPON RECEIPT WITH A MANDATORY 5% MONTHLY COMPOUNDING FINANCE CHARGE AFTER 30 DAYS. ALL FINAL INVOICES ARE NON-DISPUTABLE AFTER 30 DAYS OUTSTANDING. IN ALL INSTANCES, A 15% CHARGE WILL BE ADDED FOR THE FOLLOWING OCCURRENCES: • ALL TRAVEL, PER DIEM, AND RELATED EXPENSES INCURRED WHILE SATISFYING REQUIREMENTS. • ALL CUSTOMERS' PERSONAL EXPENSES SUCH AS HOTEL, CAR RENTAL, ETC. AS REQUESTED OF JET AVENUE AND REFLECTED ON CUSTOMER INVOICES. • ALL PASS THROUGH SUBCONTRACT EFFORTS THAT ARE OUTSIDE OF JET AVENUE INC. CORE BUSINESS AND SERVICING BUSINESS AIRCRAFT. CUSTOMER SUPPLIED PARTS WILL INCUR UP TO A 20% CHARGE (CHARGE IS BASED ON CURRENT LIST PRICE). THERE WILL BE A 4.0% CHARGE FOR CONSUMABLES, UP TO A MAXIMUM OF USD$7,500, ON ALL WORK ORDERS CONTAINING LABOR REVENUE CHARGES. THIS CHARGE WILL BE CALCULATED BASED ON THE TOTAL LABOR REVENUE MAN HOURS INVOICED. ALL WORK PERFORMED WILL BE ACCOMPLISHED IN ACCORDANCE WITH JET AVENUE INC.'S CURRENT WORK AUTHORIZATION AGREEMENT TERMS AND CONDITIONS, INCLUDING PROGRESS AND DEPARTURE PAYMENT REQUIREMENTS. CORES NOT RETURNED WITHIN 15 DAYS INCUR ADDITIONAL CHARGE. CORES SUBJECT TO BILL-BACKS FOR OVER &amp; ABOVE CHARGES. BANK TRANSFERS AND MAJOR CREDIT CARDS ACCEPTED. 4% FEE ON ALL MAJOR CREDIT CARDS. JET AVENUE INC. RESERVES THE RIGHT TO CHANGE THESE RATES AND CHARGES AT ANY TIME.</p>

            <p class="tc-section">ACKNOWLEDGEMENT AND EXECUTION</p>

            <p>BY SIGNING BELOW, EACH PARTY ACKNOWLEDGES THAT IT HAS READ, UNDERSTOOD, AND AGREES TO BE BOUND BY ALL TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF THIS ENGAGEMENT AGREEMENT, INCLUDING THE LIMITATION OF LIABILITY, CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES WAIVER, ARBITRATION, AND CLASS ACTION WAIVER PROVISIONS. CLIENT ACKNOWLEDGES THAT THESE TERMS WERE AVAILABLE FOR NEGOTIATION AND THAT CLIENT HAD THE OPPORTUNITY TO SEEK INDEPENDENT LEGAL COUNSEL PRIOR TO EXECUTION.</p>

